  note    = {FULL TEXT READ 2026-09-02. Proposes a Refugia Habitat Metric (RHM) that down-weights native species habitat suitability (MaxEnt) by invasive species suitability, negative-exponential weighting, tunable alpha/beta parameters. Case study: koura (native crayfish, Paranephrops planifrons) vs brown bullhead catfish (Ameiurus nebulosus), Aotearoa/NZ only. RHM formula is mathematically generalizable to n invasive species (Appendix A1) but case study applies it to only one invader -- not a multi-invader compounding-risk study. NOT a scoop risk (co-author Kusabs is my PhD supervisor). Bullhead catfish is already in this project's species shortlist (Section 4) -- RHM is a strong candidate methods precedent to adapt/cite for the Q5 "double jeopardy" native-refugia extension.}
}

% --- Systematic review pass 2 (search #2, 2026-09-02) ---
% NOTE: "niche overlap" in this literature usually means native-vs-invaded-
% range niche comparison for a SINGLE species (Broennimann-style), not
% multi-species spatial overlap -- a false-positive category for our
% purposes. The two entries below are the real hits: genuine multi-species,
% global, spatial-overlap mapping -- just not freshwater.

